Let $\mathcal{L}$ be a formal language, and $Th$ some set of $Th \subseteq \mathcal{S}(\mathcal{L})$ functioning as axioms. Then the inference rules of sequent calculus are 
oindent 	extbf{Theoretical Axiom:} if $A \in Th$ then $\Gamma \Rightarrow A, \Delta$  egin{center} 	extbf{G3cp} \end{center} 
oindent 	extbf{Logical Axiom:} $\Gamma, P \Rightarrow P, \Delta$ 
oindent 	extbf{Logical Rules:}  egin{multicols}{2} \[  rac{\Gamma \Rightarrow A, \Delta \quad \Gamma \Rightarrow B, \Delta}{\Gamma \Rightarrow A \land B, \Delta}	ag{$R\land$} \] \[  rac{\Gamma, A, B \Rightarrow \Delta}{\Gamma, A \land B \Rightarrow \Delta}	ag{$L\land$} \] \[  rac{\Gamma \Rightarrow A, B, \Delta}{\Gamma \Rightarrow A \lor B, \Delta}	ag{$R\lor$} \] \[  rac{\Gamma, A \Rightarrow \Delta \quad \Gamma, B \Rightarrow \Delta}{\Gamma, A \lor B \Rightarrow \Delta}	ag{$L\lor$} \] \[  rac{\Gamma, A \Rightarrow B, \Delta}{\Gamma \Rightarrow A \supset B, \Delta}	ag{$R\supset$} \] \[  rac{\Gamma \Rightarrow A, \Delta \quad \Gamma, B \Rightarrow \Delta}{\Gamma, A \supset B \Rightarrow \Delta}	ag{$L\supset$} \] \[  rac{}{ ot, \Gamma \Rightarrow \Delta}	ag{$L ot$} \] \end{multicols}  egin{center} 	extbf{G3c} \end{center}  egin{multicols}{2} \[  rac{\Gamma \Rightarrow A[y/x], \Delta}{\Gamma \Rightarrow  orall x A, \Delta}	ag{$R orall$} \] \[  rac{\Gamma, A[t/x],  orall x A \Rightarrow \Delta}{\Gamma,  orall x A \Rightarrow \Delta}	ag{$L orall$} \] \[  rac{\Gamma, A[y/x] \Rightarrow \Delta}{\Gamma, \exists x A \Rightarrow \Delta}	ag{$L\exists$} \] \[  rac{\Gamma \Rightarrow \exists x A, A[t/x], \Delta}{\Gamma \Rightarrow \exists x A, \Delta}	ag{$R\exists$} \] \end{multicols}
